WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.225
Hospital.

2
00:00:01.505 --> 00:00:05.835
Day 41 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:07.585 --> 00:00:08.609
The key idea.

4
00:00:08.889 --> 00:00:18.340
Today's goal: handle the hospital: registration, emergency, describing symptoms, admission, visiting a patient, tests, insurance and billing.

5
00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:22.033
(For a clinic visit and medicines, see Doctor and Pharmacy.).

6
00:00:23.383 --> 00:00:24.301
Watch out:

7
00:00:24.581 --> 00:00:25.882
Emergency first.

8
00:00:26.162 --> 00:00:32.093
In India, call 112 (all emergencies) or 108 (ambulance in many states).

9
00:00:32.373 --> 00:00:33.055
Say:

10
00:00:33.335 --> 00:00:35.981
I need an ambulance at address + landmark.

11
00:00:36.261 --> 00:00:38.522
A man has collapsed and isn't responding.

12
00:00:39.872 --> 00:00:40.725
Part 1.

13
00:00:41.005 --> 00:00:41.965
Key words.

14
00:00:43.215 --> 00:00:44.581
Here is a quick table:

15
00:00:44.861 --> 00:01:07.218
Word or phrase, and Meaning. reception or registration or OPD: front desk or signing up or outpatient department. emergency or casualty or ER: for urgent cases. ward or ICU or room: where admitted patients stay. admit or discharge: keep in hospital or allow to go home. consultant or specialist or

16
00:01:07.498 --> 00:01:28.383
resident doctor: types of doctors. blood test or X-ray or scan or report: tests and results. cashless or reimbursement or TPA: insurance: hospital bills the insurer or you claim later or insurance desk. visiting hours or attendant pass: when visitors are allowed or pass for the person staying.

17
00:01:29.733 --> 00:01:30.608
Part 2.

18
00:01:30.888 --> 00:01:32.104
Questions you'll ask.

19
00:01:33.354 --> 00:01:36.277
Where is the registration counter or emergency?

20
00:01:36.557 --> 00:01:38.605
Which doctor should I see for back pain?

21
00:01:38.885 --> 00:01:40.527
How long is the waiting time?

22
00:01:40.807 --> 00:01:43.474
Is this hospital cashless for insurance company?

23
00:01:43.754 --> 00:01:45.354
When will the reports be ready?

24
00:01:45.634 --> 00:01:47.063
What are the visiting hours?

25
00:01:47.343 --> 00:01:48.687
Can I stay overnight?

26
00:01:48.967 --> 00:01:52.189
What is the estimated cost of the treatment or surgery?

27
00:01:53.539 --> 00:01:55.032
When can he be discharged?

28
00:01:55.312 --> 00:01:57.701
Could you explain the report in simple words?

29
00:01:59.051 --> 00:01:59.947
Part 3.

30
00:02:00.227 --> 00:02:01.593
Questions you'll be asked.

31
00:02:02.843 --> 00:02:04.208
Here is a quick table:

32
00:02:04.488 --> 00:02:06.024
They ask, and You answer.

33
00:02:06.304 --> 00:02:07.819
Patient's name and age?:

34
00:02:08.099 --> 00:02:09.976
Ramesh Gupta, 64.

35
00:02:10.256 --> 00:02:11.429
What's the problem?:

36
00:02:11.709 --> 00:02:14.973
He has chest pain and difficulty breathing since this morning.

37
00:02:15.253 --> 00:02:16.811
Any existing conditions?:

38
00:02:17.091 --> 00:02:19.523
Yes, diabetes and high blood pressure.

39
00:02:19.803 --> 00:02:21.360
Is he on any medication?:

40
00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.709
Yes, metformin and amlodipine.

41
00:02:23.989 --> 00:02:25.035
Any allergies?:

42
00:02:25.315 --> 00:02:27.000
He's allergic to penicillin.

43
00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.645
Do you have insurance?:

44
00:02:28.925 --> 00:02:30.227
Yes, here's the card.

45
00:02:30.507 --> 00:02:31.680
Is it cashless here?

46
00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.304
Who is the attendant?:

47
00:02:33.584 --> 00:02:34.779
I am, his son.

48
00:02:36.129 --> 00:02:37.046
Part 4.

49
00:02:37.326 --> 00:02:40.078
Conversation 1: at the emergency desk.

50
00:02:41.328 --> 00:02:43.355
Here is how the conversation goes.

51
00:02:43.635 --> 00:02:44.701
Please help.

52
00:02:44.981 --> 00:02:48.096
My father has chest pain and he's sweating a lot.

53
00:02:48.376 --> 00:02:49.869
Okay, bring him here.

54
00:02:50.149 --> 00:02:51.728
What's his name and age?

55
00:02:52.008 --> 00:02:53.267
Ramesh Gupta.

56
00:02:53.547 --> 00:02:54.976
He's 64.

57
00:02:55.256 --> 00:02:56.792
When did the pain start?

58
00:02:57.072 --> 00:02:58.800
About forty minutes ago.

59
00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:00.957
It's spreading to his left arm.

60
00:03:02.307 --> 00:03:03.907
The conversation continues.

61
00:03:04.187 --> 00:03:06.129
Does he have any medical conditions?

62
00:03:06.409 --> 00:03:08.563
Diabetes and high blood pressure.

63
00:03:08.843 --> 00:03:11.446
He takes metformin and amlodipine.

64
00:03:11.726 --> 00:03:12.899
Any allergies?

65
00:03:13.179 --> 00:03:14.481
Yes, penicillin.

66
00:03:15.831 --> 00:03:17.431
The conversation continues.

67
00:03:17.711 --> 00:03:18.820
Okay.

68
00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.935
The doctor will see him right now.

69
00:03:21.215 --> 00:03:23.689
Please complete the registration at the counter.

70
00:03:23.969 --> 00:03:24.908
Thank you.

71
00:03:25.188 --> 00:03:27.151
Do you need his insurance card?

72
00:03:27.431 --> 00:03:30.567
Yes, give it to the insurance desk after registration.

73
00:03:31.917 --> 00:03:32.877
Part 5.

74
00:03:33.157 --> 00:03:36.079
Conversation 2: talking to the doctor and billing.

75
00:03:37.329 --> 00:03:39.356
Here is how the conversation goes.

76
00:03:39.636 --> 00:03:41.343
Your father is stable now.

77
00:03:41.623 --> 00:03:43.969
The ECG shows a minor blockage.

78
00:03:44.249 --> 00:03:45.615
Thank you, doctor.

79
00:03:45.895 --> 00:03:47.175
What does that mean?

80
00:03:47.455 --> 00:03:48.735
Is it serious?

81
00:03:49.015 --> 00:03:51.105
It needs treatment, but we caught it early.

82
00:03:51.385 --> 00:03:53.839
We'd like to admit him for two days for tests.

83
00:03:54.119 --> 00:03:55.057
Okay.

84
00:03:55.337 --> 00:03:56.916
What tests will you do?

85
00:03:57.196 --> 00:03:59.052
Blood tests and an angiogram.

86
00:03:59.332 --> 00:04:01.081
Then we'll decide the next step.

87
00:04:02.431 --> 00:04:04.031
The conversation continues.

88
00:04:04.311 --> 00:04:08.045
What's the estimated cost, and is it covered by insurance?

89
00:04:08.325 --> 00:04:10.330
The billing desk will give you an estimate.

90
00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:12.189
Most of it should be covered.

91
00:04:12.469 --> 00:04:13.450
At the billing desk

92
00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:19.511
Hi, I need an estimate for my father, Ramesh Gupta, admitted in ICU bed 4.

93
00:04:20.861 --> 00:04:22.461
The conversation continues.

94
00:04:22.741 --> 00:04:25.536
It's about 85,000 rupeesfor two days.

95
00:04:25.816 --> 00:04:28.312
We've sent the cashless request to your insurer.

96
00:04:28.592 --> 00:04:31.280
How long does the insurance approval take?

97
00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:33.395
Usually four to six hours.

98
00:04:33.675 --> 00:04:34.869
We'll inform you.

99
00:04:35.149 --> 00:04:36.088
Thank you.

100
00:04:36.368 --> 00:04:38.437
Could you give me the estimate in writing?

101
00:04:39.787 --> 00:04:40.726
Part 6.

102
00:04:41.006 --> 00:04:42.222
Visiting a patient.

103
00:04:43.472 --> 00:04:44.752
Which ward is Mr.

104
00:04:45.032 --> 00:04:46.312
Ramesh Gupta in?

105
00:04:46.592 --> 00:04:48.085
He was admitted yesterday.

106
00:04:48.365 --> 00:04:49.773
How is he doing today?

107
00:04:50.053 --> 00:04:51.824
Can I bring him home-cooked food?

108
00:04:52.104 --> 00:04:53.555
Is there anything he needs?

109
00:04:53.835 --> 00:04:55.776
(To the patient) How are you feeling?

110
00:04:56.056 --> 00:04:57.123
Get well soon.

111
00:04:57.403 --> 00:04:58.341
Take rest.

112
00:04:59.691 --> 00:05:00.630
Part 7.

113
00:05:00.910 --> 00:05:02.083
When things go wrong.

114
00:05:03.333 --> 00:05:04.976
We've been waiting for two hours.

115
00:05:05.256 --> 00:05:06.984
Could you tell us how long it will be?

116
00:05:07.264 --> 00:05:09.611
The bill has charges for tests that weren't done.

117
00:05:09.891 --> 00:05:12.280
The insurance approval is taking too long.

118
00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:13.776
Who can I speak to?

119
00:05:14.056 --> 00:05:15.549
I'd like a second opinion.

120
00:05:16.899 --> 00:05:17.774
Part 8.

121
00:05:18.054 --> 00:05:18.971
Practice.

122
00:05:20.221 --> 00:05:28.221
Write the 5 facts a nurse needs in an emergency: name and age, problem, since when, conditions and medicines, allergies.

123
00:05:29.571 --> 00:05:30.467
Part 9.

124
00:05:30.747 --> 00:05:31.793
Speak today.

125
00:05:33.043 --> 00:05:39.251
Write your family's emergency information in English (conditions, medicines, allergies, insurance).

126
00:05:39.531 --> 00:05:43.456
Save 112 and your nearest hospital's number in your phone.

127
00:05:44.806 --> 00:05:46.342
That's the end of this lesson.

128
00:05:46.622 --> 00:05:51.294
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

129
00:05:51.574 --> 00:05:57.675
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

